note Translated from CPython Lib/heapq.py _siftdown (lines 221 to 233).
note The leading underscore that marks the Python function private is dropped; the doc has no visibility marker outside a component's provides list.

note UNCLEAR: the doc shows headers with label words (`withdraw amount from account`) but never three bare parameters in a row; they are written side by side here
to siftdown heap startpos pos
    note GAP: a type parameter with an ordering bound - the doc only shows T on `type Queue of T`; a free operation cannot introduce T or require that items of T can be compared with "is less than"
    given heap is an editable List of T where T is Ordered
    given startpos is a Nat
    given pos is a Nat
    note UNCLEAR: Python raises IndexError if pos is out of range; the doc does not say whether `item pos of heap` needs a proof, fails, or stops the program, so no fails with line is written

    let newitem be item pos of heap
    note WORKAROUND: Python rebinds the parameter pos; the doc never sets a parameter, so a var copy is used
    var current starts at pos
    note Follow the path to the root, moving parents down until finding a place newitem fits.
    repeat while current is more than startpos
        decreases current - startpos
        note WORKAROUND: (pos - 1) >> 1 is a shift; the doc has no bit operations, so division by 2 is used, which is the same for a non-negative number
        let parentpos be (current - 1) / 2
        let parent be item parentpos of heap
        if newitem is less than parent
            note UNCLEAR: the doc never sets a list element; `set item i of list to x` is assumed by analogy with `set balance of account to ...`
            set item current of heap to parent
            set current to parentpos
            skip
        stop
    set item current of heap to newitem
